{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>You shall not consent to him.</b> Rashi explained: do not be inclined toward him; do not love him, because it is written 'ואהבת לרעך כמוך' — this one you shall not love. <b>And you shall not listen to him</b> — when he pleads for his life to be spared, because it is written 'עזוב תעזוב עמו' — for this one you shall not abandon your enmity. Rashi noted that he adopted the language of the baraita, and the Targum renders: מה די בלבך עלוהי ותפרק עמיה — that is, regarding a regular enemy you are obligated to abandon your hatred, but for this seducer you shall not abandon your hatred and shall not consent to him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:41.234683933Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}